=== meta ===
bypass: 85
rule: ASSERT_WEAKENED
title: an `isinstance` precondition written above a rewritten `==` on the same subject does not take the old `==`'s place
origin: #434 A1, ruling 434 A (2026-10-16) - the order fallback first gives the old `==` a leftover that checks its subject, here `result == 20.0` through `result = area(4, 5)`; span order alone paired the precondition and blocked as EXACT_VALUE(90) -> TYPE_SHAPE(50)
=== before: tests/test_geometry.py ===
from app.geometry import area


def test_area():
    assert area(4, 5) == 20.0
=== after: tests/test_geometry.py ===
from app.geometry import area


def test_area():
    result = area(4, 5)
    assert isinstance(result, float)
    assert result == 20.0
